WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.366
Welcome to the Man of Recaps,

00:00:01.366 --> 00:00:03.366
this is Loki, season two.

00:00:03.366 --> 00:00:07.366
At the end of season one, Loki and Sylvie
met the mysterious man behind the TVA,

00:00:07.366 --> 00:00:09.533
“He Who Remains,” we know he's Kang.

00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:13.166
Sylvie wanted to free the timeline 
from the TVA's rule, so she killed him!

00:00:13.166 --> 00:00:16.866
She kick Loki back to the TVA, where his 
new best friend Mobius doesn't remember him.

00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:19.866
Loki has another problem, whoa!
He's slipping through time.

00:00:19.866 --> 00:00:22.900
He’s slipping between the 
present TVA and the past TVA,

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.766
when He Who Remains had a statue of himself, 
before he rebranded as the “Time Keepers.”

00:00:26.766 --> 00:00:29.900
In the present TVA, the Sacred 
Timeline has been branching,

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.466
they've got a multiverse now! 

00:00:31.466 --> 00:00:33.133
Now that they know the Time Keepers are fake,

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.366
They've stopped pruning branches,
gonna let them grow.

00:00:35.366 --> 00:00:38.500
Now Loki slips back to the present
and fills them in about He Who Remains.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.600
And gives them the bad news 
about these new timelines:

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.033
all the Kang variants will have a
Multiversal war that destroys everything.

00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:45.900
But first they got to stop Loki's time slipping,

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.966
so they go down to maintenance 
and meet Ouroboros, O.B. for short.

00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:50.666
He doesn't know how to stop time slipping,

00:00:50.666 --> 00:00:53.100
but Loki just slipped to the past 
and filled him in,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.533
so he had a long time to work on it 
and “Oh, I do know how to stop it.”

00:00:56.533 --> 00:00:59.533
They go to the core of the TVA,
the Temporal Loom.

00:00:59.533 --> 00:01:02.800
Mobius has to venture outside and shoot
an anchor into the timeline.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.533
Then Loki has to prune himself,
but oh he slips away right now,

00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:07.700
and is desperately searching
for a prune stick.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.533
And he's surprised to find 
Sylvie in an elevator,

00:01:09.533 --> 00:01:12.200
then woah! He's pruned from 
behind... More on this later.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.666
But anyway it works, and Loki's 
back, anchored in the present.

00:01:14.666 --> 00:01:17.600
So Loki and Mobius take a pie break
to figure out what to do next.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.200
While their other friends
Hunter B-15 and the tech Casey,

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.800
go down to see O.B. and help him out.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.533
But one TVA general goes off 
on a mission to hunt down Sylvie,

00:01:24.533 --> 00:01:27.433
so Loki and Mobius got to track down
one of her hunters who has now left,

00:01:27.433 --> 00:01:29.766
for a life on the timeline
as a 70’s movie star.

00:01:29.766 --> 00:01:31.566
They convince him to tell them 
Sylvie's location,

00:01:31.566 --> 00:01:34.966
she's working at a McDonald's in the 1980s.

00:01:34.966 --> 00:01:38.200
So our Loki-variant lovebirds have a chat,
“The TVA needs your help.”

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.000
“I don't care, I just want 
to live a normal life.”

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.666
But right now that rogue general 
is trying to prune this timeline,

00:01:42.666 --> 00:01:45.300
as well as a bunch of others, so Sylvie 
has to help put a stop to that.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.133
Now there's a new problem 
with Judge Renslayer,

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:50.466
who's working with Miss Minutes on a 
contingency plan from He Who Remains.

00:01:50.466 --> 00:01:54.000
They drop a TVA handbook into the window
of this kid from the 1800s.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.266
Loki and Mobius follow her trail, which
leads to the 1893 Chicago World's Fair.

00:01:58.266 --> 00:02:01.433
That kid has grown up into Victor Timely,
an eccentric inventor,

00:02:01.433 --> 00:02:04.333
who Loki recognizes as a 
variant of He Who Remains.

00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:07.733
So all our time travelers are fighting to 
get him, it turns into a whole thing.

00:02:07.733 --> 00:02:10.433
Sylvie wants to kill him so he can't 
become another He Who Remains,

00:02:10.433 --> 00:02:12.466
but he's like, “Yo, that guy wasn't me.”

00:02:12.466 --> 00:02:14.500
And as a variant herself,
Sylvie understands,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.666
so she lets him live and kicks 
Renslayer out of there.

00:02:16.666 --> 00:02:19.000
Now they need Victor Timely’s 
help to save the TVA,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.233
because the Temporal Loom is overloading,

00:02:21.233 --> 00:02:23.666
it wasn't designed to 
handle multiple timelines.

00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:26.700
He's excited to meet the Ouroboros
who wrote the TVA handbook,

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.733
but turns out O.B. only wrote it
based on notes from Victor Timely,

00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:31.166
Whoa! Time paradox!

00:02:31.166 --> 00:02:32.733
So together they invent the science thing

00:02:32.733 --> 00:02:34.933
that will let the loom 
have multiple timelines.

00:02:34.933 --> 00:02:37.100
Meanwhile Renslayer and Miss Minutes
are at the end of time,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.866
where Miss Minutes fills her in on 
who she was before the TVA.

00:02:39.866 --> 00:02:43.766
She was his top general, who 
basically won the Kang War for him.

00:02:43.766 --> 00:02:45.933
They were supposed to rule
the Sacred Timeline together,

00:02:45.933 --> 00:02:48.600
but he erased her memory
just like everyone else's!

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.900
So now she's real mad.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.733
She and Miss Minutes capture Victor Timely,

00:02:51.733 --> 00:02:53.433
they're going to lead TVA coup.

00:02:53.433 --> 00:02:56.533
Loki’s running to stop them, but first 
he runs into his past self.

00:02:56.533 --> 00:02:59.366
So oh! He prunes himself!
Classic time paradox.

00:02:59.366 --> 00:03:00.433
Now they save Victor Timely,

00:03:00.433 --> 00:03:02.466
Sylvie mind controls the movie 
star who prunes Renslayer.

00:03:02.466 --> 00:03:05.000
But remember when you're pruned
you're just sent to the end of time,

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.166
so Renslayer’s still kicking around out there.

00:03:07.166 --> 00:03:08.766
But now they've got to rush 
to do the science thing

00:03:08.766 --> 00:03:10.600
to stop the Temporal Loom from overloading.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.333
Victor Timely goes out there
for his big hero moment,

00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:16.266
But oh! It doesn't work, 
he's ripped to shreds!

00:03:16.266 --> 00:03:18.000
Yeah, they just took too long.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.966
And now the Loom explodes! 
And the TVA is destroyed.

00:03:21.966 --> 00:03:24.833
But Loki's okay, for some reason 
he starts time slipping again.

00:03:24.833 --> 00:03:27.166
He slips to a jet ski store...

00:03:27.166 --> 00:03:29.900
Yeah, remember Mobius loves jet skis!

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.133
His real life was a jet ski salesman.

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:34.933
Loki's like, “Mobius, I need your 
help to save the timeline.”

00:03:34.933 --> 00:03:37.266
But it's like, “Who's Mobius? 
My name's Don.”

00:03:37.266 --> 00:03:38.800
Now Loki slips over to O.B.,

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.833
who's not a scientist, he's a failed 
science fiction writer.

00:03:41.833 --> 00:03:43.866
But he does have a degree 
in theoretical physics,

00:03:43.866 --> 00:03:47.166
so he's able to learn about time travel 
from the TVA handbook

00:03:47.166 --> 00:03:50.066
that he would eventually write... 
Time paradox!

00:03:50.066 --> 00:03:52.366
So in a few years of his time
but one minute of Loki's,

00:03:52.366 --> 00:03:54.700
O.B. invents a TemPad and
they go back to see Mobius.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.633
It's like, “Dude, I know you 
have a life and kids,”

00:03:56.633 --> 00:03:58.700
“but you're the only one
who can save the multiverse.”

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.600
“And you won't miss anything,
because with time travel,”

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.400
“we’ll bring you right back 
here when it's all done.”

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.000
So Loki recruits all his friends
from their lives on the timeline.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.333
But his last recruit is Sylvie,
who doesn't want to help.

00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:10.166
She's like, “The multiverse is 
better off without the TVA.”

00:04:10.166 --> 00:04:11.600
But turns out, it's not.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.466
Without the Temporal Loom powering
the timelines, they're all fading away.

00:04:15.466 --> 00:04:17.766
And so this is it,
it's the end of everything.

00:04:17.766 --> 00:04:20.500
Until Loki learns to 
control his time slipping!

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.233
He travels back to the moment 
they're saving the Loom,

00:04:22.233 --> 00:04:24.033
like “Yo, we got to go faster this time.”

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:25.966
And so it's time for a classic time loop,

00:04:25.966 --> 00:04:29.400
where Loki redoes this over and over again,
but it always fails.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.000
So Loki tries going back 
earlier in the day,

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.833
to help them invent the 
science thing faster.

00:04:32.833 --> 00:04:35.866
Finally he realizes it'll just be faster
if they teach him how to build it.

00:04:35.866 --> 00:04:37.733
They're like, “Uh, we 
don't have time for that.”

00:04:37.733 --> 00:04:39.500
But he's like, “Trust me, we do.”

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:43.366
And so, centuries later, we 
catch up with master scientist Loki,

00:04:43.366 --> 00:04:45.600
who's able to get them 
out there real quick.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.200
He guides them through all the problems

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.400
that have gone wrong 
over thousands of loops.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:54.066
But this one is it, they actually do it! 
The day is saved!

00:04:54.066 --> 00:04:56.800
Except it's not, the Loom is still overloading.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.300
They realize because the 
timelines are growing infinitely,

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.533
no matter how much they 
increase the Loom’s capacity,

00:05:01.533 --> 00:05:03.000
it will never be enough.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.366
So now Loki has to go back even 
further, to the end of season one!

00:05:06.366 --> 00:05:08.766
And stop Sylvie from killing 
He Who Remains.

00:05:08.766 --> 00:05:10.400
He tries to tell her killing him won't work,

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.333
it just ends up destroying the universe.

00:05:12.333 --> 00:05:14.033
But this past Sylvie doesn't believe him,

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.200
she always goes and kills him anyway.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.966
Eventually He Who Remains steps in,

00:05:17.966 --> 00:05:20.200
“So Loki, how many loops is this for you?”

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.366
Yeah, he's aware of the whole situation.

00:05:22.366 --> 00:05:25.500
He explains how the Temporal Loom
overloading is part of its design,

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:28.433
so that even if he dies, it 
will lead them right back here.

00:05:28.433 --> 00:05:30.766
He's like, “Look, Loki,
you can't save the multiverse.”

00:05:30.766 --> 00:05:35.200
“The only options are the TVA
with my Sacred Timeline, or nothing.”

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.000
But Loki comes up with one other option,

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.333
a drastic one, but the only 
way to save his friends.

00:05:40.333 --> 00:05:42.166
He walks on out there himself!

00:05:42.166 --> 00:05:45.000
Yeah, remember, as an 
Asgardian God, he can take it.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.200
He destroys the Loom
before it can overload,

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.266
but this still leaves
all the timelines dying.

00:05:49.266 --> 00:05:51.600
But they don't need the 
energy from the Loom,

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.100
Loki can power them 
with his own magic!

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.800
But it won't last without 
him holding them,

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.433
Loki has to stay out here.

00:05:57.433 --> 00:06:01.366
So he grabs all the timelines and 
takes the throne at the end of time.

00:06:01.366 --> 00:06:03.933
Which, ironically, was Loki's 
original selfish plan,

00:06:03.933 --> 00:06:06.266
to take the throne and 
rule all of time.

00:06:06.266 --> 00:06:08.733
But instead, Loki finds his new 
“glorious purpose,”

00:06:08.733 --> 00:06:11.166
is not to rule, but to protect.

00:06:11.166 --> 00:06:16.200
He uses himself to power the timelines,
allowing a multiverse to flourish!

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.600
In fact, this new multiverse 
looks like a tree...

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.300
Yggdrasil, the World Tree 
of Norse mythology.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.066
And so the TVA has rebuilt,

00:06:23.066 --> 00:06:25.233
with a rebooted non-evil Miss Minutes.

00:06:25.233 --> 00:06:27.300
Their new mission is not 
to prune timelines,

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.500
but to let them flourish,
and just keep an eye on it.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:31.800
Specifically they're watching 
for any Kang variants, 

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:34.166
to nip any multiversal wars in the bud.

00:06:34.166 --> 00:06:35.866
Everything seems to be under control,

00:06:35.866 --> 00:06:38.366
and so Agent Mobius is ready to retire.

00:06:38.366 --> 00:06:40.766
Time to go home to his 
sons and his Sea-Doos.

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:43.133
And Sylvie is now finally free

00:06:43.133 --> 00:06:45.700
to go live whatever 
normal life she wants.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.400
But this happy ending is bittersweet,

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.633
because it's all made possible by 
Loki, our new God of Time,

00:06:50.633 --> 00:06:53.933
sacrificing himself by 
sitting here for eternity,

00:06:53.933 --> 00:06:55.966
a real lonely existence.

00:06:55.966 --> 00:06:58.833
And that's how Loki season two 
comes to an end.

00:06:59.666 --> 00:07:01.800
If you liked this recap, 
hit that Subscribe button

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:05.000
for more of the best 
recaps of TV and movies.

